author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Native isolated controls distinguish a missing executable from an installed child that deliberately exits 127 or prints not found.; Classification uses actual resolution and recognized runner context, preserving shell syntax, Windows semantics, exit codes, stderr and aggregate counts; arbitrary child ENOENT text is not sufficient.; Public SDK, CLI and MCP result contracts and documented recovery agree."
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Classify proven shell lookup failures as setup failures while preserving child assertion semantics.
expected_result: A missing literal executable is spawn_error with the original exit code and stderr; executed children exiting127 or printing ENOENT remain assertion failures.
actual_result: "Linked95-test cohort passes, including actual native shell controls and POSIX/Windows resolver boundaries. Hosted native Windows regression and all six packed first-run platform/runtime checks pass at58e8f1226; aggregate exact coverage passes100/100/100/100. First-head static planner metadata failure is corrected locally; revised-head required checks and review remain pre-merge gates."
